1. Create a New Project:
Open your terminal and create a new directory for your project:

mkdir vue-component-wrapper
cd vue-component-wrapper

2. Initialize a package.json File:
Run the following command to create a package.json file:

npm init -y

Step 2: Install Vue.js

    Install Vue.js:
    Install Vue.js as a dependency:

npm install vue



Install Your Pre-Bundled Component:
Install the npm package that contains your pre-bundled JavaScript:

npm install your-pre-bundled-package

Step 3: Create Your Vue Component

    Create the Component:
    Create a src directory and add your Vue component file (e.g., MyWrapperComponent.vue):

mkdir src
touch src/MyWrapperComponent.vue


Write the Component Code:

Open src/MyWrapperComponent.vue and write the Vue wrapper for your pre-bundled component:

<template>
  <div>
    <!-- Use your pre-bundled component here -->
    <div id="pre-bundled-component-container"></div>
  </div>
</template>

<script>
import YourPreBundledComponent from 'your-pre-bundled-package';

export default {
  name: 'MyWrapperComponent',
  mounted() {
    // Initialize your pre-bundled component
    YourPreBundledComponent.init('#pre-bundled-component-container');
  },
  beforeDestroy() {
    // Clean up your pre-bundled component (if needed)
    YourPreBundledComponent.destroy();
  },
};
</script>

<style scoped>
/* Add any styles here */
</style>


Step 4: Create an Entry Point

    Create an Entry File:
    Create an index.js file in the src directory:



 touch src/index.js

 Export the Component:
Open src/index.js and export your Vue wrapper component:

import MyWrapperComponent from './MyWrapperComponent.vue';

export default MyWrapperComponent;

// Optional: Export as a plugin for global registration
export const MyPlugin = {
  install(Vue) {
    Vue.component('MyWrapperComponent', MyWrapperComponent);
  },
};


Step 5: Bundle the Vue Component

Since your pre-bundled JavaScript is already packaged, you only need to bundle the Vue wrapper component. You can use a simple bundler like Vite or Vue CLI for this.
Option 1: Using Vite

    Install Vite:


    npm install --save-dev vite

Create a vite.config.js File:

touch vite.config.js


Add Vite Configuration:
Open vite.config.js and add the following configuration:

import { defineConfig } from 'vite';
import vue from '@vitejs/plugin-vue';

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [vue()],
  build: {
    lib: {
      entry: './src/index.js',
      name: 'MyWrapperComponent',
      fileName: 'my-wrapper-component',
    },
    rollupOptions: {
      external: ['vue'],
      output: {
        globals: {
          vue: 'Vue',
        },
      },
    },
  },
});



Add a Build Script:
Open package.json and add a build script:

"scripts": {
  "build": "vite build"
}

npm run build



